A||||15||Formula||Octane for over 11:1 compression?||||1||
Z||000000||Formula||09-29-2001||06:50 PM||||The fiero is pinging at idle..<P>I'm pretty sure they put the 11:1 compression pistons in it with shaved heads.  So assuming its an actual 11:1. What octane should I run?  It has 94 in it now and is pinging at idle.  I'm assuming I'll have to make a trip out to the local airport for gas?  Should 11:1 be ok with 100 octane or will I need 105+ ?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Formulasigs.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroRacer||09-29-2001||08:07 PM||||Try retarding your ignition settings.  Installing improved cooling equipment like a 160 degree thermostat or a 175 degree fan switch.||||reg||6
Z||000002||baldlobo||09-29-2001||08:07 PM||||it either the airport or one of two other options, either an octane booster of your choise or alcohal injection  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leper||09-29-2001||08:54 PM||||As a general rule for an iron block/head motor. Move the decimal point of the compression one place to the right.<BR>So 11 to 1 would need about 110 octane.<BR>That rule usually applies to big v8's and the 2.8 has a really small bore compared to them so you might be able to get by with a litte less octane. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||09-29-2001||09:09 PM||||Use water wetter or some other heat transfer agent as well if you are not already. Faster heat transfer from the cc will also help. If the retard and cooling system changes don't solve it, you might be able to to richen the fuel mix or add water injection. 11:1 is not so ridiculous as to be unworkable.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||09-30-2001||02:00 AM||||Thanks, I'll be going out to the airport monday.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierowrecker||09-30-2001||02:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>The fiero is pinging at idle..<P>I'm pretty sure they put the 11:1 compression pistons in it with shaved heads.  So assuming its an actual 11:1. What octane should I run?  It has 94 in it now and is pinging at idle.  I'm assuming I'll have to make a trip out to the local airport for gas?  Should 11:1 be ok with 100 octane or will I need 105+ ?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Formula!<BR>Pull your plugs and see what color they are...<BR>If they are white, you need to enrichen the mixture...<BR>Sounds like it is too lean...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||09-30-2001||07:26 AM||||Check mixture and timing first, failing that, head for the airport  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Red Line water wetter in the cooling system helps.<P><BR>If you have a Cat, don't get anything withought specifically "UNLEADED" in the name, do not get 'LL' anything...<P>A friend of mine has a mustang that we rebuilt a 351W motor to ~11:1compression (STOCK is 10:1...)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000008||Formula||09-30-2001||10:09 AM||||The mixture is rich, and we can't get it timed.  I was told that if its pinging then it can't be properly timed.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Bazooka||09-30-2001||09:34 PM||||Formula,<BR>    I use TORCO Racing Fuels, Accelerator- Race Fuel Concentrate (unleaded). One quart to a full tank of gas brings me from 93 octane to 107+ octane. A higher concentration can give you your 110 octane. Its about $15 a quart but I get no ping. You can store this a lot easier than aircraft fuel.<BR>***************************<BR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR>[B]Thanks, I'll be going out to the airport monday.<BR>***************************<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Tina||09-30-2001||09:48 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B> the local airport for gas?  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just be careful....<BR>Avgas is not the same stuff you get out of the pump at the local gasststion, it's missing some important additives.<BR>If you do end up using it, be sure to mix it with Marvel fuel additive for top end lubricant, or pump fuel.<P>Tina<BR>383 Stroker<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 09-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fierowrecker||09-30-2001||11:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>The mixture is rich, and we can't get it timed.  I was told that if its pinging then it can't be properly timed.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>???<BR>You do know about the jumper when timing?<BR>Or is the timing jumping about when you try to set it?<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000012||pontiacs4me||10-01-2001||01:21 AM||||what cam are you using?  If you have alot of overlap intake pressure can bleed through the exhaust before the exhaust valve closes, which doesnt always yeild your optimum compression ratio.  And did you polish the inside of your combustion chambers?  Doing that cuts down on octane tolerance also.  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Formula||10-01-2001||02:00 PM||||I dont think jumping the computer would help, as the computer is in my bedroom  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I need to get the specs on this freakin engine so I can get it to max potential.  <P>The timing is way off, I think the Cam might have been degreed so that TDC is not the same.  Its running over 20 degs advanced right now.  If I rotate the distributor it wont run right either so I assume its in the right notch.  If I try to run 10 deg advanced it barely will run and it wont even start.  but 20 and above make it run fast, but it is pinging and after it revs up to 4 or 5k it starts bogging down from the timing being so far off.  We have the secondaries running right and everything so I can assume its not them.  I have it down to the carb jetting, igniton, timing, or fuel.  And if the fuel was making it ping at idle then I couldnt time it so Im hoping the fuel is my problem.   btw, where can I buy the stuff that you add to make it 107 octane?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Formula_sigx21.gif"> ||||reg||1
